{"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":260394,"title":"File:Raccoon (Procyon lotor) 2.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Raccoon_%28Procyon_lotor%29_2.jpg/960px-Raccoon_%28Procyon_lotor%29_2.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raccoon_(Procyon_lotor)_2.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Raccoon (<i>Procyon lotor</i>)."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2005-08-05"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benutzer:Darkone\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"de:Benutzer:Darkone\">Darkone</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 2.5"}}}]},{"pageid":11053499,"title":"File:Radiometer 9965 Nevit.gif","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/28/Radiometer_9965_Nevit.gif?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Radiometer_9965_Nevit.gif","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Radiometer. The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crookes_radiometer\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Crookes radiometer\">Crookes radiometer</a>, also known as the <b>light mill</b> or solar engine, consists of an airtight glass bulb, containing a partial vacuum. Inside are a set of vanes which are mounted on a spindle. The vanes rotate when exposed to light. The reason for the rotation has been the cause of much scientific debate. 640x480, 240 fps"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2010-07-30"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Nevit\" title=\"User:Nevit\">Nevit Dilmen</a> (<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Nevit\" title=\"User talk:Nevit\"><span class=\"signature-talk\">talk</span></a>)"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}}}]},{"pageid":12427243,"title":"File:Raftsundet panorama, 2010 09.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Raftsundet_panorama%2C_2010_09.jpg/960px-Raftsundet_panorama%2C_2010_09.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raftsundet_panorama,_2010_09.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"A view to Raftsundet and mountains such as Trolltindan from Hinnøya (Lofoten) in September 2010."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"September 2010 (28 September 2010, according to <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exif\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Exif\">Exif</a></span> data)"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Ximonic\" title=\"User:Ximonic\">Ximonic</a>, Simo Räsänen"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}}}]},{"pageid":20157380,"title":"File:Raccolte Extraeuropee - Passaré 00095 - Maschera cimiero Ejagham - Nigeria.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Raccolte_Extraeuropee_-_Passar%C3%A9_00095_-_Maschera_cimiero_Ejagham_-_Nigeria.jpg/960px-Raccolte_Extraeuropee_-_Passar%C3%A9_00095_-_Maschera_cimiero_Ejagham_-_Nigeria.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raccolte_Extraeuropee_-_Passar%C3%A9_00095_-_Maschera_cimiero_Ejagham_-_Nigeria.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Crest mask. The wooden head is covered with animal skin and is on a base of woven fibers which serve as linkage with the costume. The realistic oval face is light colored, with red lips and eyebrows. The mouth is open showing the teeth. On the top two black-dyed horns.\n<p>The Ngbe society, among the Ejagham of the Cross River, is a secret society of warriors holding commercial and political functions. The membership is built around a set of shared symbols, including masks.\n</p>\nUsually masks are covered with antelope skin but there are also human skin masks, therefore the scholar Leo Frobenius assumed that warriors originally did not wear a mask on their heads, but the head of a killed enemy. Thus the mask is interpreted as a form of appropriation of the power of the dead."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"20<sup>th</sup> century<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P571,+1950-00-00T00:00:00Z/7</div>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}}}]},{"pageid":20424980,"title":"File:RAF Eurofighter Typhoon.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/RAF_Eurofighter_Typhoon.jpg/960px-RAF_Eurofighter_Typhoon.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RAF_Eurofighter_Typhoon.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Royal International Air Tattoo  2012"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2012-07-07 17:14:02"},"Artist":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/people/39463459@N08\">Peter Gronemann</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 2.0"}}}]},{"pageid":26871164,"title":"File:RAF Search and Rescue Helicopter in the Cairngorms MOD 45155350.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/RAF_Search_and_Rescue_Helicopter_in_the_Cairngorms_MOD_45155350.jpg/960px-RAF_Search_and_Rescue_Helicopter_in_the_Cairngorms_MOD_45155350.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RAF_Search_and_Rescue_Helicopter_in_the_Cairngorms_MOD_45155350.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"A <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Air_Force\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Royal Air Force\">Royal Air Force</a> (RAF) <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Search_and_Rescue\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Search and Rescue\">Search and Rescue</a> (SAR) helicopter with D Flight <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No._202_Squadron_RAF\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:No. 202 Squadron RAF\">No. 202 Squadron RAF</a> from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RAF_Lossiemouth\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:RAF Lossiemouth\">RAF Lossiemouth</a> is pictured during a training exercise in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cairngorm\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Cairngorm\">Cairngorm</a> mountain range in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scotland\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Scotland\">Scotland</a>.  Royal Air Force Search and Rescue crews train throughout the year at different locations and in different weather conditions.\n<ul><li>Object name: is-5768-hr</li>\n<li>Organisation: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Air_Force\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Royal Air Force\">Royal Air Force</a> (RAF)</li>\n<li>Supplemental categories: Equipment, Aircraft, Helicopters, Sea King, Operations, Fire SAR</li>\n<li>Keywords: Royal Air Force, RAF, equipment, helicopter, Sea King,  HAR3A, squadron, Sqn, search and rescue, SAR, 202 Squadron, 202 Sqn, RAF Lossiemouth, mountain, cold, winter, Cairngorms</li>\n<li>Country: Scotland</li></ul>"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2013-01-12 18:18:17"},"Artist":{"value":"SAC Faye Storer"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"OGL v1.0"}}}]},{"pageid":39102354,"title":"File:Radovljica Linhartov trg drei Blechblasinstrumente 19032015 0925.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Radovljica_Linhartov_trg_drei_Blechblasinstrumente_19032015_0925.jpg/960px-Radovljica_Linhartov_trg_drei_Blechblasinstrumente_19032015_0925.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Radovljica_Linhartov_trg_drei_Blechblasinstrumente_19032015_0925.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Baritonhorns, exposed on Linhart square in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radovljica\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Radovljica\">Radovl